{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Good</b> — like \"turn back, O good man,\" like \"all, many nations,\" for everything is sound in our language. Or its meaning is \"how good,\" and thus \"it is good\" — he is a man who grants grace. And he said חונן (grants grace) to follow after the Name, for He is חנון (gracious). And the word יכלכל is doubled, like וכל בשליש." "<b>With justice</b> — as is fitting to do. And some say: יכלכל (will sustain) is like \"he will sustain his sickness.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 112, :notes {0 "The prooftexts cited elliptically are Judges 19:5 (הפוך איש טוב) and Obadiah 1:2 (כי הכל נכון / כל רבים עמים); וכל בשליש is obscure, possibly a fragmentary citation; rendered hyper-literally.", 1 "The comparison יכלכל מחלהו appears to allude to Isaiah 53:4 (ומחלינו מכללותינו); rendered hyper-literally as Ibn Ezra cites it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:33.449136645Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}